---
arrangement: why-address-unmatched
when-used: The whole `dorc why <addr>` render when the address matched no analyzed command. Value: the address as given.
why: law-lineno-identity: the ONE line-number space is the source file's, so an unmatched address says so rather than silently reporting the wrong surface.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork tune --profile web

-- replay --
$ dorc why nosuchcommand --book=book.sh
dorc why: no analyzed command matched nosuchcommand (an address is a SOURCE line:
`<book>:<N>` or a bare `<N>`).

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: why-address-unmatched
{{v0}} = "nosuchcommand"
